In article <23rlgk$360@saturn.haverford.edu> awerner@ralph.cs.haverford.edu (Alex Werner) writes:

>-A ring of vampiric regeneration. While wearing it, you would get half of the
>HP of physical damage you inflicted to other people added to your HPs

	This is something I've been wondering about nethack.  Shouldn't
this be something that Stormbringer does?  If I remember correctly, Elric
used Stormbringer to give him extra energy so he wouldn't need all his potions
to survive as an albino.  Stormbringer would drain life energy from it's
victims and give some of it to Elric.  This could be implemented similar to
the luck system, you could gain extra HP from monsters as you killed them but
the extra points you received would eventually go away.  You could even have
it set up to reduce the level it goes back down to.  I.e. start with HP of
100, use Stormbringer to get up to 150, over the next 3000 moves, with no
fighting, HP goes back down to 95.  Something like -1 base HP for every 10 HP
you gain from Stormbringer.  I also think (if it's not already implemented,
which I think it may be) that Stormbringer should randomly attack monsters
around you and not let you run away until they (or you) are dead.  Perhaps
this could be implemented such that the more you use it, the more likely it
will beserk on you.  You could even add in some really special effects, like
the ability to summon it after using it a lot, or the ability for Stormbringer
to attack things on it's own, or force you to attack monsters even when you
are not wielding/carrying it.  (I.e. you leave it locked up in some chest
while you go down to the local shop to buy some stuff, but surprise, surprise!
Stormbringer is extra berserky and breaks out of the chest, flys into your
hand and starts attacking the shopkeeper!!!)

	Speaking of Elric tales... how about a potion of leather skin.  There
was one story where Elric and co. made up a special potion that gave them extra
tough skin so they could endure some test/trickery....  It was only temporary
of course!!


